---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FinalCTA from '~/components/FinalCTA.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '~/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About · Vicji Massage"
  description="Victor's story: a Brazilian therapist who traveled to Thailand to study Thai Massage at the source. Now practicing in Itacaré, Bahia."
  lang="en"
  path="/en/about"
>
  <section class="py-24 sm:py-32">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="label-overline mb-4">The story</div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-5xl sm:text-6xl text-ocean mb-12 leading-tight">
        From Thailand to India, and home to share what I learned.
      </h1>

      <div class="aspect-[3/4] sm:aspect-[16/10] rounded-2xl mb-12 relative overflow-hidden bg-ocean-dark">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/photos/portrait-meditative.webp" />
          <img
            src="/photos/portrait-meditative.jpg"
            alt="Victor in a meditative moment during a session"
            class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </picture>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-ocean-dark/40 via-transparent to-transparent"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-soft space-y-6">
        <p class="font-display italic text-2xl text-ink leading-snug">
          Thai Massage is an ancient practice of healing, respect, compassion, and care for the other. Its benefits go far beyond the physical body, and can be felt for days after a session.
        </p>

        <p>
          My name is Victor. I am Brazilian, and massage came into my life as a question before it became my profession. I wanted to understand how the body holds the experiences of life, not always positive ones, like fears, tensions, and traumas, and the way those situations affect people, to the point of manifesting physically in the body. And at the same time, to discover how to unmake all of that, and find peace and freedom to live in harmony from the right kind of care.
        </p>

        <p>
          That question took me to Thailand, where I trained as a massage therapist, right at the source of the tradition. I learned traditional Thai practice: pressure along the energy lines (sen), passive stretches, meditative pace, working with the breath, and the spiritual dimension that holds it all together. I learned that massage was born integrated, and not fragmented.
        </p>

        <p>
          From there I went to India, where I immersed myself in yoga. I deepened my understanding of the body as an energetic system: the chakras, the flows, the blockages, and what makes a practice actually heal. Between these two formations, I lived many experiences around the world that shaped how I see the body, energy, and presence.
        </p>

        <p>
          I came back to Brazil because I felt this work was missing here. We live at a pace that hurts the body in layers, and most massages on the market only treat the physical symptom, not the root of the problem. Today, I am the only practitioner in Brazil offering this integrated approach: traditional Thai Massage technique combined with the energetic understanding I carry with me.
        </p>

        <p class="font-display italic text-xl text-ink leading-snug">
          A word about price.
        </p>

        <p>
          This work is physically demanding. To deliver a 2h or 3h session with full presence, I take care of my own body every day. I practice yoga, I keep a slow pace of life, I rest between sessions. I see only a few clients per week because each one asks for a complete offering, and I don't want to give less than that.
        </p>

        <p>
          The price I charge reflects all of this: the training at the source of the tradition, years of practice, the care I take of my body so I can care for yours, and the real time each session requires. It is not the price of a spa massage because it is not the work of a spa. It is something else. Those who understand the difference find value. Those looking for something quicker and more superficial find it in many places, and that is okay too.
        </p>

        <p>
          Every session I give is an extension of what I learned: presence, intention, and respect for the body. No rush. No empty technique. A complete offering.
        </p>

        <p class="font-display italic text-xl text-ink-muted">
          Khòp khun kráp 🙏<br />
          With love and presence,<br />
          Victor
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="divider-ornament"></div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-sand-deep/30">
          <div class="label-overline mb-2">Thailand</div>
          <p class="text-ink">
            Massage therapist training
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm mt-2">
            Traditional Thai Massage, learned at the source of the tradition.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-sand-deep/30">
          <div class="label-overline mb-2">India</div>
          <p class="text-ink">
            Yoga formation
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm mt-2">
            Understanding the body as an energetic system. Chakras, flows, spiritual practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-sand-deep/30">
          <div class="label-overline mb-2">World</div>
          <p class="text-ink">
            The only one in Brazil
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm mt-2">
            Offering this integrated approach of traditional massage combined with energetic practice.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FinalCTA lang="en" />
  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/en/' },
    { name: 'About', href: '/en/about' },
  ]} />
</BaseLayout>
